    Trim dead weight and document the stack for newcomers
    
    Fat removed:
    
    - packer/downloaded_iso_path/ held a 2.8 GB Ubuntu ISO, committed. It is
      Packer's local download cache and is not even used: iso_download_pve = true
      makes Proxmox fetch the ISO server-side. .gitignore had "packer/*.iso", which
      does not match a subdirectory, so it slipped through. Untracked here and the
      pattern fixed; the blob still sits in local history (see below).
    - variables.auto.pkrvars.hcl at the repo root was never loaded -- Packer reads
      *.auto.pkrvars.hcl from the template directory, and builds run from packer/.
      It had drifted from the real file (ssh_username "jreboll" vs "ubuntu",
      unresolved REPLACE_WITH placeholders) and was missing iso_datastore_id
      entirely, so it would have failed had anything read it.
    - .gitignore listed variables.auto.pkrvars.hcl.example, contradicting the fact
      that the example is tracked on purpose for people to copy.
    
    Bugs found while reviewing:
    
    - kubernetes_repo_version was plumbed from the pkr.hcl variable through
      environment_vars, sudoers env_keep, and sudo, and then discarded: the script
      hardcoded KUBERNETES_REPO_VERSION on line 4. It now honors the passed value
      with a fallback, so the variable does something. HOLD_KUBERNETES_PACKAGES
      gets a fallback too, since `set -u` would abort if it went missing.
    - `sudo -E` was in execute_command but sudo rejects it and only warns; env_keep
      is what actually carries the variables. Dropped, and documented so it does
      not get "fixed" back in.
    - Cluster nodes ran CPU model qemu64 -- the provider default, which silently
      overrides the template's cpu_type. qemu64 predates x86-64-v2, so Calico
      v3.32's v2-only binaries crash-looped and left every node NotReady. Added
      var.cpu_type (default "host"); this is an in-place change, though the VM
      needs a stop/start for a CPU model change to take effect.
    
    Docs: rewrote the root README around the two-stage build-then-deploy flow,
    added terraform/README.md, and commented the parts that are opaque without
    context -- the boot_command keystrokes, cloud-init's role, why provisioners
    only run at creation, and why /tmp must not be cleaned by a script running
    from /tmp.
    
